# 2026-09-19 measurement hygiene (MegaTower, rules for reading every row in this file):
#   * A gated+timed run is +0.211 ms slower than the SAME BINARY timed alone (18.598 bench-only
#     vs 18.809 --validate --bench, three interleaved reps, spread 0.006).  Split by
#     -DPFX_VALALLOC=1 (allocate the ~100 MiB of validate-only fp32 dump buffers and never
#     validate): footprint 0.144, the validation pass itself 0.067.  The deployable number is
#     the bench-only one; gate in one invocation and time in another.
#   * There is NO warm-up effect on this part: fresh containers read 18.598/18.597/18.600/18.599
#     four runs deep, and soak length is worth +0.02 from n=100 to n=1500.
#   * Placement is worth up to 0.097 ms: -DPFX_ARENA_SKEW=<bytes> (burn N bytes at the front of
#     the arena, never touched) sweeps 18.582 at 16 MiB to 18.679 at 256 KiB.  No skew is pinned
#     -- the curve moves whenever an allocation does -- but any single-arm claim below ~0.1 ms
#     must control for it.  r6's pad passes that control: pad on 18.599, pad off 18.668, pad off
#     + an equal-sized front skew 18.689, so the pad's win is a stride effect and not an address
#     shift (MegaSched's isolated down GEMM agrees: 1.2-1.5 %, masked but not redundant).
# 2026-09-19 r15b: the two cuts in ONE node (PFX_MID_DYN=2).  One ranking pass per camera
#   serves both budgets and writes both index vectors; the second top-k, the O(MIDV) index
#   search and the containment counter are all gone, because a token kept at TKEEP has rank
#   < TKEEP <= MIDV and its mid coordinate IS the first cut's compaction counter.  The two
#   compaction offsets come from group scans rather than per-item "sum the flags below me"
#   loops.  370 launches, 18.596 vs mode 1's 18.633/18.643 and r14's 18.495/18.509 in the same
#   interleaved session; same index-for-index acceptance, same digit.
#   Cost split by ablation (-DPFX_NOSCORE=1, a pricing knob whose keep set is meaningless):
#   DPAS score + reduce = 0.035 ms, selector + both stages' tables = 0.055 ms.
# 2026-09-19 r15 (MegaTower): the hybrid's BOTH cuts are now produced ON DEVICE from one
#   score, so the chunk is ARGUMENT-FREE again -- no --mid-keep/--post-keep, nothing uploaded
#   per observation.  Seven graph nodes (score DPAS + reduce, top-192/cam, top-128/cam of the
#   same score, the two index vectors, and both stages' RoPE/kmask tables), 372 launches,
#   +0.130 ms over r14's host-uploaded sets (18.630/18.639 vs 18.497/18.510, interleaved).
#   ACCEPTANCE: with the keep files supplied for comparison the device's own vectors are
#   index-for-index IDENTICAL to them -- `[midsel] dmid==host 1 (448 of 448), dpost==host 1,
#   containment violations=0` -- and the chain digit is the same 6.5938e-03 with the files
#   absent, which is what proves the device selection IS the gated selection.
#   r14 (host-uploaded keep sets, 365 launches, 18.51) is reproducible with:
#     PI05_XFLAGS="-DEX_SCBF16=0 -DPI05_MEGA_EXPERT=1 -DSG_EPI2=1 -DSG_APF=1 -DSG_SLMFIT=1 -DSG_WL1_AGRP=0 -DSG_WL1_QKV=0 -DPFX_DNPAD=16 -DPFX_GU_PERSIST=1 -DMEGA_KDB=2 -DPFX_QKV_PFD=2 -DPFX_QKV_AKD=64 -DMEGA_ATTN_LIFT=1 -DMEGA_PFWG_DOWN=1 -DMEGA_PFWG_DN3=1 -DPFX_GU_FINE=1 -DPFX_PRUNE_LAYER=0 -DPFX_MID_KEEP=192 -DPFX_MID_ALLOC=1"
#   plus --mid-keep/--post-keep; it is the faster row but it is not deployable.
# 2026-09-19 r14 (MegaTower + MegaPrefix): the HYBRID prune schedule is now the shipped
#   geometry -- 192 visual tokens/camera kept from Gemma layer 0 (a 448-row mid stream for
#   layers 0..2) and the layer-0 score's top-128/camera thereafter (320 rows, layers 3..17).
#   18.515 ms against r13's 18.978 in the same interleaved session (-0.463; three reps each,
#   spread 0.005), 1500-replay soak clean, chain digit RE-PINNED to 6.5938e-03 against the
#   two-stage reference share/ref/case2_hybrid192_128{,_w4}.
#   Also in r14: `down`'s weight-panel pad stride is now DATA (`pfx::LayerW::dn_pad`), so the
#   mid layers pack plain (dp_pf = 0 inverts deep prefetch at 448) while the 15 post layers
#   keep r6's pad -- worth 0.079 ms, measured, and NOT retired.  peer/prefix_stage.hpp
#   46045985 fixes the three `down` paths that ignored the pad entirely; the must-fail control
#   is `pad on + dp_pf = 0` (1.0368e-01 on the old header, 6.5938e-03 on the new one).
#   The default REQUIRES --mid-keep/--post-keep until the two-stage device selector lands.
# TOOLING PINNED TOO (MegaPrefix, 2026-09-19): mbc's build_fused.sh was a FORK
#   (52b2a70a vs 983cea8f) with NO XFLAGS handling at all, so every flag A/B of the
