#   8.1872e-02 / keep EQUAL 256/256 P=426 / sem_nk 570/570, hist3 keep-forced 3.3697e-02, hist3 ring
#   2.5259e-02 with keep DIFFER 226/256, proj.out 1.7326e-02 and siglip.out 4.1057e-02, T=128 s00 devkeep
#   2.3183e-02, LiberoHc14's AT=10 real LIBERO frames 2.8652e-02 / 2.4291e-02 / 2.6172e-02 and his AT=15
#   DROID devkeep with the flag compiled ON 2.2206e-02 / 8.1872e-02 / P=426.
#   THE FIRST FORM IS VOID: -DSG_LNQ_GB=2 (sg.ln 0.372, -0.103, and -0.047 in LiberoHc14's AT=10 chunk) moves
#   the DROID chain to 2.3794e-02 -- OUTSIDE the 2.2e-02 bar -- while making the tower BETTER (proj.out
#   1.7130e-02, siglip.out 4.0691e-02); hist3 4.5453e-02, hist3 ring 3.4113e-02 with keep DIFFER 230/256.
#   Four-arm control: GB=1 (cache hints only) is character-identical, so the replacement load form is exact;
#   GB=4 (hoist before the epilogue loop, no hints) moves the digit identically to GB=2.  What moves it is
#   hoisting the loads to a point where mean and rstd are already live, which lets IGC contract
#   (v - mean) * rstd * gw + gb differently.  Two rules out of it: "same bytes, same expression, same order"
#   is NOT a bit-identity argument on this stack (source order is not instruction order), and the effect is
#   INPUT-dependent -- GB=2 is character-identical on three real LIBERO frames at tv=10 and moves the DROID
#   comparators at tv=58/46, so a numerics-capable flag is not "bit-identical" until BOTH checkpoints'
#   comparators have run.
