#   extractor prefix, never retyped (full argv in raw/build-*.argv.txt):
#     fused_mux_droid   3a75ec281c1a3875b0cd1fbe9cd547247bdbb1af5457a27a805c9097bb63eb3c  (AT=15, windows 64/128/256)
#     fused_mux_libero  5f6eb480b8888c508bffd8c062f446ec1bdbdefd36d95fb7aca87ffa2fa5fdb2  (AT=10, windows 64/128/256)
#     fused_t64         5cba6453e25cbf4410cf0434d95c71c79eeaa62c20ccd2e7072d8acbf38e5a3b
#     fused_t128        a50e9a80cd494d2723b65ff3060663de9e6cd0ce1b850afdb1f5531de1e132f1
#     fused_t256        9eae70554a7423c79899e71c68aa2f99676b3de25d5a38cfb40ef7025a5ad4b0
#     fused_libero      4e3389dc7a622d886cecaef85a849586c6843b78e11145c1eec5730103b03e39
#   fused_t64 came out BYTE-IDENTICAL to LiberoHc15's independently built `d_pfall`
#   (5cba6453e25cbf44, his receipt S7) -- two boxes, two scripts, same bytes.  That is a
#   stronger statement than a matching digit and it is not guaranteed on this AOT toolchain
#   (the farm is still not byte-reproducible on every TU), so it is recorded, not relied on.
#   GATE: DROID on billy card0 (PCI 0000:03:00.0) beside SimRuns' resident server, LIBERO and
#   both serve paths on rafael (PCI 0000:10:00.0), ssog-b580:neo2513, lock nest
#   gpu0.lock -> .gpu0.lock -> .ram.lock, ONE --validate per invocation, nothing timed.
#   EVERY figure below is CHARACTER-IDENTICAL to the digit its rung lane published; the mux
#   geometry and the standalone control built from the SAME tree agree on every row.
#     T64   s00 devkeep  2.2206e-02 / max_abs 8.1872e-02 / keep EQUAL 256/256 P=426 / sem_nk 570-570
#           hist3 ring   2.5259e-02 / 6.5959e-02 / keep DIFFER 226/256 P=328 / sem_nk 558-558
#     T128  s00 devkeep  2.2374e-02 / 7.3123e-02 / EQUAL 256/256 P=426 / 570-570
#     T256  s00 devkeep  2.3690e-02 / 7.4463e-02 / EQUAL 256/256 P=426 / 570-570
#     LIBERO AT=10 libero10-ep0010  s00 2.8652e-02 / s01 2.4291e-02 / s02 2.6172e-02,
#           keep EQUAL 256/256 P=413 / 362 / 333, sem_nk 522-522, 85 stages / 2 binding failures
#   proj.out 1.7326e-02 and siglip.out 4.1057e-02 on every DROID row.  rc=1 on the binding
#   2.0e-02 FP32 gate is this line's normal state on a real-frame reference (0d rule 15).
#   SERVE-PATH BIT-IDENTITY (rafael, the deployed path, DEVICE's own selection, no --keep-force
#   because a keep-forced chunk cannot depend on the ring): three geometries resident in one
#   process, arena 3472.8 + 751.4 + 281.7 = 4505.9 MiB, setup 6.2 / 1.2 / 0.4 s, and every
#   routed chunk bit-identical to an independent single-window --acc-out control -- including
#   the ring carried 58 -> 87 -> 58 -> 200 across THREE window boundaries and back
#   (e2 vs cold 2.0519e-02, e3 vs cold 2.2147e-02, e4 vs cold 1.1618e-02), text_valid 300
#   REFUSED rather than truncated, t64/t128/t256 rc=0.  AT=10 serve: same, routed to T=64.
# 2026-09-23 RE-PIN (ServeTune, evidence/servetune-20260923/RESULTS.md).  src/fused.cpp ->
#   96ac3478: the --serve path's per-text_valid RETUNE becomes a CACHE.  FinalSpeed 11.3
#   measured the retune as the largest served-minus-bench term (2.58 ms of a 20.8 ms served
#   chunk on a stream that changes text_valid on 61 % of chunks).  The six host-built device
#   tables (pre-prune RoPE cos/sin, pre-prune kmask, the expert's kv_bias and action RoPE, the
#   hoisted K_sem_nk count) are now built ONCE per distinct text_valid into their own device
#   buffers and kept resident BESIDE that text_valid's recorded graph, in one cache entry
#   bounded by the existing --graph-cache: an executable graph bakes buffer ADDRESSES into its
#   kernel arguments, so tables and graph must live and die together.  A change event is then a
#   pointer rebind (bpre/bsem tables + sem_nk) plus a 9 KiB device-to-device refresh of the
#   three expert tables -- those cannot be rebound, because mega_expert_stage_prepare()
#   snapshots `s.a.ex.k = P.k` at setup and only re-applies kv_k/kv_v/noise/actions per launch.
#   `rope_tables` (pow+cos+sin over TPRE x HH = 81 920 entries) no longer runs per chunk, and
#   nothing is uploaded on a hit.  Second change, same block: the served chunk did THREE
#   submit-and-wait round trips (H2D -> wait -> replay -> wait -> D2H -> wait); make_queue()
#   builds the queue with sycl::property::queue::in_order, so the two intermediate waits are
#   redundant and are now taken only if q.is_in_order() is false.  212 added / 63 removed lines,
#   16 hunks, all inside `if (serve)` except the --graph-cache doc comment -- which is why every
#   gate digit below is character-identical to FinalBuild's.
#   BUILD: buildfarm, ssog-b580:neo2513-aot, oneAPI DPC++ 2025.2.0, AOT bmg-g21 -doubleGRF,
#   fb_build.sh with every flag line read out of THIS file (MUX_WINDOWS=64,128,256):
#     fused_mux_droid   db89756ca6b0451040cbbf6e3490d28606d5ed510de3d4cc371bfce3259d6edb  (AT=15, windows 64/128/256)
#     fused_mux_libero  a52d55a6dfcfd6b59ed84300f6eb3129b77411b504561b2c6f53a9bef20b97e3  (AT=10, windows 64/128/256)
#     fused_t64         4329f288269fb40e30598970a8ae8457d5b3707d209e5711aad84918403219b3
#     fused_t128        6b89f367b798055cd8462c3403302e8806b37a3a3609bf205b18fd892392df39
