#   GATE: sleepy-joe card1 (PCI 0000:09:00.0), ssog-b580:neo2513, lock nest gpu1.lock ->
#   .gpu1.lock, ONE --validate per invocation, nothing timed in a gated process.  All 14 rows
#   (7 mux + 7 matched control) are CHARACTER-IDENTICAL to the FinalBuild entry above:
#     T64   s00 devkeep  2.2206e-02 / 8.1872e-02 / keep EQUAL 256/256 P=426 / sem_nk 570-570
#           hist3 ring   2.5259e-02 / 6.5959e-02 / keep DIFFER 226/256 P=328 / sem_nk 558-558
#     T128  s00 devkeep  2.2374e-02 / 7.3123e-02 / EQUAL 256/256 P=426 / 570-570
#     T256  s00 devkeep  2.3690e-02 / 7.4463e-02 / EQUAL 256/256 P=426 / 570-570
#     LIBERO AT=10 libero10-ep0010  s00 2.8652e-02 / s01 2.4291e-02 / s02 2.6172e-02,
#           keep EQUAL 256/256 P=413 / 362 / 333, sem_nk 522-522, 85 stages / 2 binding failures
#   SERVED-BYTE IDENTITY, which is the claim a gate cannot make (the gates never enter the
#   serve path): every chunk's actions.f32 over the FULL sets, hashed and diffed against the
#   3a75ec28 / 5f6eb480 binaries on the same card -- 435/435 DROID and 360/360 LIBERO
#   BYTE-IDENTICAL, and again byte-identical at --graph-cache 8, which forces 71 evictions and
#   so exercises the free-and-rebuild path.  PI05_TV_CACHE_VERIFY=1 (debug env: rebuild the
#   tables on the host on EVERY hit and memcmp them against the resident set) over both sets,
#   two passes each: 651 hits compared, 0 mismatches.
#   TIMING (same card, same session, interleaved in both orders, n=435/360, min_freq pinned
#   2850 and restored to 1200): the per-change-event cost goes to zero and the served row drops
